ADVERSARIAL PASS (step 3, items a-e). Every one measured, none taken from the design.

(a) AN MCP CALLER CANNOT REJECT. The allowlist test's denominator arm is foreign-red ("expected 19 to be 17"), so the membership itself was probed directly rather than inferred from a red file. Probe source, run and deleted in the same command:

    import { expect, it } from "vitest";
    import { MCP_EXCLUDED_COMMAND_KINDS, wiredMcpToolKinds } from "./mcp-tool-allowlist.js";
    it("an MCP caller cannot reject a plan", () => {
      expect(MCP_EXCLUDED_COMMAND_KINDS).toContain("approval.decide_intent");
      expect(wiredMcpToolKinds()).not.toContain("approval.decide_intent");
      expect(wiredMcpToolKinds()).not.toContain("approval.decide");
    });

-> Test Files 1 passed (1) / Tests 1 passed (1). The exclusion is DERIVED, not hand-kept: `MCP_EXCLUDED_COMMAND_KINDS` = OPERATOR_PRINCIPAL_KINDS less `session.open` (mcp-tool-allowlist.ts:73-85), so REJECT rides the operator-only wire by construction and cannot drift back onto the roster without the vocabulary changing first.

(b) REJECT TWICE ON THE SAME RUN REFUSES, with the code and the layer both pinned, and the arms are green (approval-intent.test.ts, Test Files 1 passed / Tests 94 passed): a second REJECT of a REJECTED run -> {code: "APPROVAL_RUN_NOT_REVIEWABLE", layer: "APPROVAL_RUN_BINDING"}, an APPROVE of that same run refuses under the same tuple, and exactly one PlanningRunRejected event remains (:1570-1585). A separate arm covers REJECT AFTER an APPROVE (:1587-1607): same refusal, run event count unchanged, the goal's event list byte-identical before and after.

(c) REJECT THE SUCCESSOR AGAIN -> A SECOND SUCCESSOR, RESOLVER HOPS 2. Proven LIVE, not in a fixture: reject #2 (decision dp 840, cmd 8b5e3f7f) targeted run-5e2b5ff2405040692b392f0d whose own state.runKind is REVISION, and minted run-364badebfb47fdf2e0631b57 (REVISION, v1) on the same goal. The offer ladder followed it: the gate came back bound to the second successor (dump s14-gate-third) and the APPROVE landed on it (graphApprovalRef approval:run-364badebfb47fdf2e0631b57). The goal's immutable planningRunRef never moved.

(d) THE APPROVE PATH IS BYTE-IDENTICAL. Across the whole feature (bb1afdf6^..HEAD) the production wire apps/daemon/src/planning/approval-intent.ts changed by 15 insertions and 1 deletion — the single deleted line is an `import` refactored into approval-intent-rejection.ts; not one APPROVE-flow line was removed. In the test file the feat commit's ONLY deletion is a REJECT arm being re-aimed ("refuses a REJECT carrying no reason before any durable read"); 71718982 deleted nothing; 0965b1e1 deleted only helper/import lines it replaced. Zero APPROVE arms deleted or weakened, and all 94 pass.

(e) A REASON CANNOT BREAK THE MISSION FENCE. rejection-instructions.test.ts + rejection-instructions-fence.test.ts = Test Files 2 passed (2) / Tests 29 passed (29), and the live recomposition against the UnAI store printed "fence check: markers in mission = 2" with the operator's text inside the block (comment-0320e151).

ONE MORE, NOT ON THE LIST AND THE REASON THE ROW GREW: the feature's PLAN_REJECTED state did not end at the approval. Found by the live drive, fixed, drilled — comment-cc3145c5.
